{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Now he was the provider for all the people of the land</b> It is not fitting that the overseer of the land, second to the king of Egypt, would be personally selling a se'ah or a tarkav of grain to each and every person. Therefore our Rabbis were moved on this point and said (Genesis Rabbah 91:6) that he ordered all the storehouses sealed except for one at that time. And according to the plain sense, it is plausible that people came before him from all the lands, and he would inquire and investigate about them and issue orders to the officers: sell to the people of such-and-such a city this much and this much grain of such-and-such a kind. And Jacob's sons were required to come before him among those arriving from the land of Canaan to give orders concerning them — how much would be sold to their land — for they were the first of those who came from the land of Canaan, and they came before him on behalf of all of them."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "תרקב (tarkav) is left as a technical measure; it is variously understood as a unit of dry measure in rabbinic sources."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:43:48.747894448Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}